    {
      "blockId": "tour:body:47f6c11f40afc686",
      "field": "body",
      "sourceTextSha256": "dd67e6ec246b4639a43462ebdb0fda115ccd17970a9709cc7c91719649a160ba",
      "text": "\n**Duration:** 10 days / 9 nights  \n**Dates:** 12 February 2027 – 21 February 2027  \n**Route:** Rio de Janeiro, 3 nights + Foz do Iguaçu, 3 nights + Búzios, 3 nights  \n**Format:** group tour with an English-speaking guide\n\n## Prices and hotels\n\nPrices are in US dollars per person for the full programme. SGL means single occupancy, DBL double occupancy and TRP triple occupancy. Breakfast is included in all options; hotels may be replaced by others of the same category.\n\n| Category | Rio de Janeiro | Foz do Iguaçu | Búzios | SGL | DBL | TRP |\n|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 3* | ibis Copacabana Posto 5 | Viale Tower | Rio Buzios Beach | $5 425 | $3 550 | $3 540 |\n| 4* | Windsor Leme | Vivaz Cataratas Deluxe | Rio Buzios Boutique | $6 580 | $4 065 | $3 878 |\n| 5* | Miramar by Windsor | Doubletree by Hilton Foz | Rio Buzios Boutique Deluxe sea view | $7 825 | $4 980 | $4 465 |\n\nCarnival tickets and hotel – Sambadrome – hotel transfers are included in the price. International flights and domestic flights Rio – Iguazu – Rio are paid separately; domestic flights cost from $500 per person.\n\n## From Carnival night to the beaches of Búzios\n\nIn Rio, you have 2 excursions of 4 hours each: a cable-car ride to Sugar Loaf with a walk through the old centre, and a train ride through the Tijuca Forest to Corcovado. On the evening of Day 2, you head to the Sambadrome, where samba schools, costumes and moving floats fill the night. Tickets and the return transfer to your hotel are already included in the programme.\n\nYou spend the next 3 nights in Foz do Iguaçu. The Brazilian trails offer panoramic views of the cascades, while the Argentine walkways bring you closer to the rushing water and the Devil’s Throat. You can add the Macuco Safari, Bird Park or a flight over the falls at an additional cost.\n\nThe final 3 nights are devoted to Búzios. After flights and excursions, there is time for the ocean, the peninsula’s different beaches, a boat trip or a buggy ride. The transfer from Rio airport to Búzios and the return to the airport on the final day are included.\n",
